From 8f882c5a1e20a12b74443c9429aa1a2071388126 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: johnnylibretexts <264531926+johnnylibretexts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 00:36:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(a11y): carry CXone pageID on review sections,
 extract TOC build/merge

Accessibility review sections are currently built inline inside
importA11YSectionsFromTOC and keyed only by sectionTitle. Two consequences:

- A section records no page identity, so anything downstream that wants to
  address a CXone page has only its URL to go on.
- Merging a re-imported TOC matches on title alone, so a retitled page loses
  every answer already recorded against it.

Extract the traversal and merge into server/util/a11yreviewutils.ts:

- buildA11YReviewSectionsFromTOC walks children/subpages, skips malformed
  entries, and records pageID from the TOC node's id/@id.
- mergeA11YReviewSectionsFromTOC matches existing sections by URL first and
  falls back to title, consuming each existing section at most once, and
  refreshes title/URL/pageID while preserving recorded review state.

Both are covered by unit tests, run with `npm test` in server/ via the node
test runner.

Also widens a11ySectionReviewSchema with the per-section scan fields
(wcagReview, dojExceptions, remedyStatus, remedyLastScannedAt, remedyFindings,
remedyWcagSummary, remedyError) and adds Project.remedyAdaptLastScan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
